I always wear a ring of levitation and then just zero in on it that way.
It usually takes me less than 200 turns from the start of the Plane.
But usually is four times (the first couple I did it the hard way).

> Five I need to figure out how to keep my tamed monsters alive between
> planes

I've never been happy relying on pets through the planes. If you have a
magic whistle, blow it a couple of times and see who comes with you, but
if you have a large number of pets, you're going to get some attrition.
Then again, people ascend with their original pet (or at least talk
about it), and I brought a dog I generated in the VotD all the way to
the altar once, so it's clearly doable.

> Six there has to be something better than a unicorn horn to cure
> illness

As another poster mentioned, noncursed extra or full healing, or blessed
healing if you've got that, or cure sickness spell. Or --- just Finger
or Wand of Death Pestilence and don't worry about it.

> Seven If I hadn't tried this I'm sure I would have died (might still
> do).

You never know until you get there, but quite possibly, yes. :)

> Eight maybe I'm expecting too much from conflict

Conflict, in my opinion, seems to serve to decrease the damage you are 
taking per round, since fewer things are attacking you. If you're lucky,
priests and player monsters will off one of the Riders for you, too. 
Conflict does not cause you to win Astral, but it helps. On the other 
hand, if you're carting as many pets up as you can, conflict is obviously
going to cause problems with that strategy. In that case you are counting
on your pets to soak hits for you instead, I think. Maybe someone else 
can describe that strategy better?

